1
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,357
The End of the Sea Did you know there's an

2
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,617
awesome treasure hidden
at the end of the sea?

3
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:23,337
And anyone who finds it,
the King of the Pirates!

4
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,877
Is that exciting or what?

5
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:28,607
There are incredible adventures
out there just waiting for us!

6
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:35,757
Bon voyage, have the
courage to sail and believe.

7
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,657
And we will see a glimpse of

8
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:43,660
the sun rising on our tomorrow?

9
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:51,037
Back when we first started,
we had separate horizons.

10
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:55,817
Sailed toward different dreams,
things have changed now.

11
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:00,417
For together we found, we looked
through the spyglass and see.

12
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,957
And we know that our hearts
have brought us here.

13
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,657
Where the conscious points our destiny.

14
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:13,520
There's no looking back,
take the hell with me!

15
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:20,120
Bon voyage, we can't stop all
our troubles, forget the past.

16
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:24,637
Though the future's
unclear, we still can smile.

17
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:27,337
We know we'll get there.

18
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:29,020
No regrets.

19
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:32,837
Every tear that we've cried only helps.

20
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,300
Our dreams come true.

21
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:40,200
You and those dreams
are precious in my life.

22
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:47,020
A glimpse of the sun
rising on our tomorrow.

23
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:57,950
Hey!

24
00:01:58,033 --> 00:01:59,387
That's the wrong way, Zoro!

25
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,920
We're supposed to be going west!

26
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,600
You know, west, this way?

27
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,297
Jeez, I can't believe
your sense of direction.

28
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:08,100
But he's going east.

29
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,417
Oh, come on, Luffy.

30
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,237
Use your head for something
besides a hat rack for a change.

31
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:14,277
We're supposed to go to
the skull's right eye,

32
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:16,654
so we gotta go right, you rubber brain!

33
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,397
Why don't you go tell
those two heroes that we're

34
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:21,997
supposed to be heading south
before they end up lost?

35
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:23,139
Sure thing, Robin.

36
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,420
Luffy! Zoro! Wait up, guys!

37
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,630
South, huh?

38
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,584
You should have said so sooner.

39
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,224
Luffy, that's a pretty
neat stick you got there.

40
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:52,830
Isn't it?

41
00:02:52,913 --> 00:02:53,743
It's mine, though.

42
00:02:53,826 --> 00:02:54,656
You gotta get your own.

43
00:02:54,739 --> 00:02:55,569
Isn't it?

44
00:02:55,652 --> 00:02:56,482
It's mine, though.

45
00:02:56,565 --> 00:02:57,395
You gotta get your own.

46
00:02:57,478 --> 00:02:58,800
Aww, I want one.

47
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,680
Stick! Stick!

48
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,580
What's up with sticks?

49
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:04,370
You know,

50
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:09,620
I thought this course would be scarier,
but so far, it's been nice and peaceful.

51
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:15,940
Hey, Chopper, you're in
a pretty good mood today.

52
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,897
You feeling courageous for a change?

53
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:19,100
Yup, you betcha.

54
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,860
I feel so safe with these guys.

55
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,520
Yeah, you're right.

56
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:28,177
The forest really has
been a big disappointment.

57
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:30,117
Not to admit birds and trees for two whole

58
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,800
days makes me want to scream I'm so bored.

59
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:35,337
We haven't even seen
one of Eneru's priests,

60
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:38,740
so I know exactly how you
feel, Chopper. Do you?

61
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,125
Just listen to the two of you.

62
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:46,438
Are you that eager for
something dangerous to happen?

63
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,350
What in the hell?

64
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:08,263
What in the hell?

65
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:22,957
Wind, good.

66
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,100
Helm, good.

67
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,000
This is so nice.

68
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:29,749
It's just like a pleasure cruise,
but we're making bad time.

69
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,577
Navigator, pick up the pace!

70
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:33,397
I'm afraid we can't, Captain Usopp.

71
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,217
The Milky Road gets
pretty steep in places,

72
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:38,980
so we have to rely on
dial power to get by.

73
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,592
Pour it on, little crow!

74
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:43,260
Sanji, you are my official bodyguard.

75
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,997
The captain is afraid
of this creepy forest.

76
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,786
Come on, for crying out loud.

77
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,897
The only person I'm planning on
protecting is my little Nami.

78
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:53,837
Hey, it's about time for that
weird knight's medicine, isn't it?

79
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,397
Do you remember where Chopper
said he was gonna put it?

80
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,310
Excuse me, dear.

81
00:04:57,393 --> 00:04:58,600
My name is Gonfong.

82
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,060
That's Gonfong.

83
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:01,477
Oh, yeah, that's right.

84
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,177
I think he left it sitting on
a barrel down in the galley.

85
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:05,907
Can you grab it, Nami-sweet?

86
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,750
Old man.

87
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,742
Shall I tell you a little
of this land's history?

88
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,460
You back again, old man?

89
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:23,840
Get out now!

90
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,140
Enough, Wiper.

91
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:29,360
Gonefall is here to negotiate.

92
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:30,990
Negotiate what?

93
00:05:31,073 --> 00:05:32,900
No, Chief. We're through.

94
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,657
We're not going to stand
by while two old men

95
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:39,034
negotiate away everything we
fought for our whole lives.

96
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,000
Listen, Gonfall.

97
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,173
You can forget about any kind of treaty.

98
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:47,940
If you want compromise so
badly, then give it all back.

99
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:52,397
For generations we've watched you sky
people slaughter us like little pigs.

100
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,310
Enough!

101
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:56,117
And now you're saying that
you want to make peace?

102
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,030
Ha!

103
00:05:57,113 --> 00:05:59,097
I cannot give it all back to you.

104
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:02,617
The power of the Upper
Yard's birth is of the utmost

105
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:06,080
importance to every man and
woman now living in Scypia.

106
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,520
All are grateful for its many blessings.

107
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:12,700
I have no right to take that away.

108
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:15,500
These people are, after all, innocent.

109
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,404
Oh, so the Scypia people
are innocent, are they?

110
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:22,097
I guess you can call them
that since they let you do

111
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:25,057
their fighting for them and
never bloody their own hands.

112
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:27,697
Maybe it's time we involved
a few innocent people.

113
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:29,480
I won't allow that.

114
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:31,200
You want peace so badly.

115
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,480
Make a sacrifice.

116
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,057
Execute a hundred of
your own innocent people

117
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:37,477
on the ancient altar and
bring us their heads.

118
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,390
You're mad.

119
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,540
I won't.

120
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,840
Then we're done talking.

121
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:48,240
Get lost, or I'll take your
head as a down payment.

122
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:51,820
Wait, wiper.

123
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:56,860
Be careful when you use my name, old man.

124
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:04,280
I am quite fond of the juice
made from your pumpkins.

125
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,480
I'll kill you!

126
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:10,450
Wiper, stop!

127
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:12,120
Warriors, restrain him!

128
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,780
What is this? Kamakiri!

129
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,540
Braum, not you two!

130
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:28,616
Aisa cries a lot, doesn't she, Nurse?

131
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:35,180
Yes, she always cries when there's
a disturbance in the village.

132
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:38,660
It's Wiper, right?

133
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:52,337
I really don't know but
you have to admit when

134
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,077
there are problems in
the village he's right

135
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:56,797
in the middle of them
why what do you think of

136
00:07:56,880 --> 00:08:02,480
him Lock I think that
he frightens me as well

137
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:04,960
he's like a demon

138
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:19,970
The...

139
00:08:20,053 --> 00:08:20,883
The Fourth!

140
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,110
Wiper!

141
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,820
I told you before!

142
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,017
That's Isha's treasure!

143
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,453
You have no right to...

144
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:30,857
But Brahm...

145
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:34,177
We can't assume we'll get
another chance like this.

146
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:36,800
I won't let this opportunity pass.

147
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,924
If you don't think you're
up to it, stay behind.

148
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,000
I won't hold it against you.

149
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,122
Don't say that.

150
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,220
You know we're up to it. Are you?

151
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:50,500
Are you up to abandoning anyone
who falls during the battle?

152
00:08:57,200 --> 00:09:02,600
If you can step over the bodies of
your dying comrades and keep fighting,

153
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:03,920
then follow me.

154
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:10,100
Now, I swear, Enoru's head is mine.

155
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:17,240
Until six years ago, I was gone.

156
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:20,219
Uh, did you hit your head, old man?

157
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,700
As you have no doubt learned,

158
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:28,997
it is believed that the Upper Yard first

159
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:33,520
appeared in Skypiea abruptly
a good 400 years ago.

160
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:38,680
Until then, Skypiea had always
been a peaceful Sky Island.

161
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:45,197
Items from the Blue Sea that were
occasionally brought here by the

162
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:49,280
knock-up stream were rare and
valuable treasures to the Sky people.

163
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:50,870
Likewise,

164
00:09:50,953 --> 00:09:55,371
all of the Fourth on the Sky Islands
was brought here by the knock-up stream.

165
00:09:56,740 --> 00:10:00,057
But a quantity of Fourth
as vast as the upper yard

166
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:03,800
appearing in the sky seemed
like an unimaginable miracle.

167
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:14,500
The Sky People were understandably
overjoyed and worshipped it as holy ground,

168
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,920
a gift from heaven itself.

169
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:22,940
But the original inhabitants
were still on that birth,

170
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,540
and a war erupted over its possession.

171
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:30,320
Those inhabitants were the Shandians.

172
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,129
Then they're the gorillas?

173
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:33,730
So,

174
00:10:33,813 --> 00:10:35,417
you're saying the Shandians used to live

175
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,577
on Jaya when it was still in the Blue Sea?

176
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:38,490
That's right.

177
00:10:38,573 --> 00:10:41,497
The current blasted them into
the sky against their will.

178
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:46,217
Hold on, does that mean that you just
stole the land that was rightfully theirs?

179
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,130
It does.

180
00:10:47,213 --> 00:10:51,720
The Sky People's greed drove them
to steal the Shandorians' homeland.

181
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:53,800
And for the last 400 years,

182
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:58,337
the war between the Shandians and the
Sky People has gone on without a break.

183
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:01,817
The Shandians are simply trying
to regain their lost home.

184
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:02,920
How sad.

185
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:05,500
All those lives lost. Wait a second!

186
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:07,660
Doesn't that make you the bad guy?

187
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,580
I'm sorry.

188
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,140
But I'm afraid that's correct.

189
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:17,980
Oh, my medicine.

190
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,575
Excuse me, I almost forgot to take it.

191
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:24,080
What about Eneru?

192
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:26,060
Who's he?

193
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,240
What's his story?

194
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,420
While I was still gone,

195
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:38,657
he appeared from another Sky
Island, leading a group of warriors.

196
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:42,622
They dealt a heavy blow to my
Divine Squad and to the Shandians.

197
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:45,389
Then they seized control
of the Upper Yarn.

198
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:47,420
That was six years ago.

199
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:50,637
Since then nearly all the
Divine Squad have been

200
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,840
enslaved and forced to
perform some mysterious labor.

201
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:55,472
I don't know what it is.

202
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:59,617
But the Shandians don't care who God is.

203
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:03,641
They want what they've always
wanted, the return of their homeland.

204
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:06,840
Yeah, right.

205
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,637
If all these Shandians are interested
in is getting their homeland back,

206
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:13,597
then why did they attack
us the minute we showed up?

207
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:17,057
The members of the Divine
Squad sometimes steal a

208
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:20,560
ship in hopes that they might
escape from Enderu. However,

209
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:23,877
the Shandians still consider
the Divine Squad enemies,

210
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:26,017
and they will eliminate them on sight.

211
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,276
They must have mistaken you for them.

212
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:30,480
Oh, of course.

213
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:32,251
That makes it all better.

214
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:36,357
One reason I became the Sky
Knight was to help these

215
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:39,500
escapees make it safely
away to other Sky Islands.

216
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:42,917
There is no place on
the Upper Yard that such

217
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,529
outlaws would be able
to avoid Eneru's eye.

218
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,897
To hear the way you tell it,

219
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:50,274
this Eneru guy sounds like
he must be the devil himself.

220
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:52,850
For all we know,

221
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:55,717
he's out there right now listening to
every word we're saying and taking notes,

222
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:56,630
notes, notes!

223
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,997
Oh, you gotta be kidding me.

224
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:00,597
Hey, don't tell me you've
suddenly become a convert.

225
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:03,400
Hey, you heard what the
old man said. Scary.

226
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:04,840
The devil himself?

227
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:07,800
No, but he comes very close.

228
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:14,400
Eneru has decreed that all outsiders
like yourselves are criminals.

229
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,790
What's more,

230
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:20,586
he has made the inhabitants of Skypiea
responsible for leading them to judgment.

231
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:27,460
This gives rise to the
islander's sense of guilt.

232
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:33,980
When the people believe they
are committing a criminal act,

233
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:36,100
they become overwhelmed by it.

234
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:37,920
It weakens their will.

235
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,840
Eneru knows this and exploits it.

236
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:44,460
He has created a flock of
helpless lambs to rule over.

237
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:48,397
The lives of the people
are like playthings to him.

238
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,760
The devil indeed.

239
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:57,897
When we landed on Angel Beach we thought
we'd found something like a paradise.

240
00:13:57,980 --> 00:13:59,780
Boy were we wrong!

241
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,417
Of all the places that
ancient city of gold

242
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,717
could have ended up being
this is just our luck.

243
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:06,630
Oh!

244
00:14:06,713 --> 00:14:11,277
That's right this city
you sure were excited

245
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:15,580
about it but please tell
me something what is gold?

246
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,457
Run for it!

247
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,040
It's a giant snake!

248
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,437
It's enormous.

249
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:35,814
I wonder if it's another
result of the environment here.

250
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:46,898
Okay, Catfish Face, it's
time for you to get belayed.

251
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:58,771
How in the hell can something
so big move so freaking fast?

252
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:22,780
Uh, change of plan. We're running away.

253
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:24,240
Sounds good.

254
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:31,100
Don't let that venom
touch you! It's death!

255
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:38,790
Oh!

